---
// Withheld reads — the publication's own basket (docs/discovery-design.md, feature 11).
// Every record this publication could not read reliably from the filings, each with its
// specific reason. The subject of every row is this publication's reading, never the reader
// and never the business: nothing here says what a company is, only that WE could not read
// its record. Alphabetical, because the absence of a read has no magnitude to sort. The rows
// come from readability.mjs, the same record the company-page strip shows, so the two can
// never disagree; withheld records still appear in the catalog and on their own pages, which
// are reading surfaces — this list labels them, it does not hide them.
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import fundamentals from "../../data/fundamentals.json";
import adr from "../../data/fundamentals.adr.json";
import jp from "../../data/fundamentals.jp.json";
import adrRatios from "../../data/adrRatios.json";
import rates from "../../data/rates.json";
import { readabilityOf } from "../../lib/readability.mjs";
import { dataAsOf, fmtAsOf } from "../../lib/freshness.mjs";

const pools = [
  ...(fundamentals.companies || []),
  ...(adr.companies || []),
  ...(jp.companies || []),
];

const rows = [];
for (const c of pools) {
  const rec = readabilityOf(c, adrRatios, rates);
  if (!rec) continue;
  const tk = String(c.ticker || "").toUpperCase();
  if (!tk) continue;
  rows.push({
    ticker: tk,
    name: c.name || "",
    href: c.market === "JP" ? `/jp/${tk}` : `/c/${tk}`,
    reasons: rec.reasons.map((r) => r.text),
  });
}
rows.sort((a, b) => a.ticker.localeCompare(b.ticker));

const refreshed = fmtAsOf(dataAsOf);
---

<BaseLayout title="Withheld reads, Owner Scorecard">
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Withheld reads</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The records this publication could not read reliably from the filings, each with the
      specific reason. The limitation stated on every row is ours — a fact about our reading,
      not about any business.
    </p>
    <p class="sub">
      A record lands here when a read the site runs everywhere else could not be run honestly:
      too few readable years, a balance sheet whose lines contradict one another, an ADR whose
      dollars-per-ADS bridge is missing a verified term. Rather than guess, the reads were
      withheld and the reason is published. These companies keep their pages and their place in
      the catalog; they are absent from the test lists, never shown there as failing. What any
      business is, and what it is worth, remains your judgment alone.
    </p>
    <p class="order">Alphabetical, because the absence of a read has no magnitude to sort.</p>
    {refreshed ? <p class="dateline">From the latest filings · data as of {refreshed}.</p> : null}
  </header>

  <div class="countBar">
    <span class="total">{rows.length.toLocaleString()} {rows.length === 1 ? "record" : "records"}</span>
  </div>

  <ul class="rows">
    {rows.map((r) => (
      <li>
        <a class="tk" href={r.href}>{r.ticker}</a>
        <span class="nm">{r.name}</span>
        <span class="why">{r.reasons.join("; ")}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="foot">
    Each reason is the same guard the company page and the test lists already apply; this page
    collects what those guards withheld, so the unreadable is labeled rather than hidden. When a
    later filing makes a record readable, the row leaves this list on the next data refresh.
  </p>

  <style>
    .hero h1 { margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .lede { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 10px; max-width: 68ch; }
    .sub { color: var(--ink-dim); margin: 0; max-width: 72ch; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 14.5px; }
    .order { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin: 10px 0 0; }
    .dateline { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); margin: 6px 0 0; }

    .countBar { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); margin: 20px 0 0; padding-bottom: 7px; }
    .total { font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink); }

    .rows { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .rows li { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .tk { font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; flex: 0 0 64px; }
    .nm { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
    .why { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-dim); flex: 0 0 auto; text-align: right; max-width: 56%; white-space: normal; line-height: 1.5; }

    .foot { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 12px; max-width: 78ch; line-height: 1.6; }
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .rows li { flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .nm { flex: 1 1 auto; }
      .why { flex: 1 1 100%; text-align: left; max-width: none; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
